  "final_message": "I haven't made the change, because the premise doesn't hold: `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced`.\n\n- **Required field:** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` parses the event with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. A missing `channel` throws `ContractViolationError`, and the whole event is rejected.\n- **Stored and tested:** `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes `channel` to the `orders` table. The README lists it in the `OrderPlaced` contract, and `analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88` has a test that \"requires channel\".\n- **Effect of removing it:** once orders-service stopped sending `channel`, analytics-ingest would reject every `OrderPlaced` event.\n- **Billing:** `billing-service` doesn't use it. Its test at `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` passes `channel: undefined` and works.\n\nIn orders-service, `channel` appears in `core/order.ts`, `core/events.ts` and `api/requestParsing.ts`. It also appears in the tests, in `README.md`, and in the `POST /orders` example in `CLAUDE.md`. It's also part of the public `POST /orders` request body.\n\nHow do you want to go ahead?\n1. **Coordinate first:** analytics-ingest, owned by another team, stops requiring `channel`, and then we remove it here. I can write up the change they'd need.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and API only:** `OrderPlaced` would keep emitting `channel`. This needs somewhere else to get the value, so it doesn't work unless the model still holds it.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now:** I'd do this knowing analytics-ingest will break until they ship their side.",
